            0.646,
            0.042,
            0.848,
            0.059
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Journey Inside the Atom"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.857,
            0.018,
            0.952,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "N 159"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.087,
            0.775,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Explain and arrange the following statements in the correct chronological order to show how atomic models have evolved over time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.142,
            0.775,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Bohr’s model proposed that electrons move in fixed orbits around the nucleus, each with a definite energy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.176,
            0.774,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Thomson’s model depicted the atom as a ʻplum puddingʼ with electrons embedded in a sphere of positive charge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.21,
            0.774,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Rutherford’s model proposed that atoms have a dense central nucleus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.243,
            0.685,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Dalton’s model described atoms as indivisible particles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.263,
            0.774,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Electrons move around the nucleus in orbits. Why do they not fly away from the atom? Explain what keeps them attracted to the nucleus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.301,
            0.774,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Assertion (A):  The discovery of subatomic particles helped in understanding the atomic structure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.338,
            0.773,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reason (R): The number of electrons is equal to the number of protons in an atom."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.375,
            0.389,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Choose the correct option:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.394,
            0.725,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.411,
            0.752,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.428,
            0.398,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) A is true, but R is false."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.445,
            0.398,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) A is false, but R is true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.465,
            0.776,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Magnesium is essential for many biological processes, including muscle contraction. For an atom of magnesium with a mass number of 24 and atomic number 12, determine the number of (i) protons, (ii) neutrons, (iii) electrons, and also illustrate the arrangement of electrons in a magnesium atom."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.553,
            0.748,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Find the following information for the elements shown in Fig. 8.17:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.575,
            0.384,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Name of the element"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.597,
            0.267,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Symbol"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.618,
            0.428,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Total number of electrons"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.64,
            0.454,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Number of valence electrons"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.662,
            0.401,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) Valency of the element"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.684,
            0.37,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vi) Number of protons"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.706,
            0.338,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vii) Atomic number"
            }
          ]
        },
